    "grammarFocus": "Idiomatic: приходить в голову (to occur to someone)",
    "hints": [
      "This is a fixed idiom using a motion verb. Which prefixed motion verb means 'to come/arrive' and combines with 'в голову' to mean 'to occur to'?"
    ],
    "explanations": [
      "'Приходить/прийти в голову' (to come to mind, to occur to someone) is a fixed idiom. 'Пришла в голову мысль' = a thought occurred to me. Other prefixes change the meaning entirely: уйти (to leave), выйти (to exit), дойти (to reach)."
    ],
